# IC-7300MK2 CI-V command catalog extracted from IC-7300MK2_ENG_CI-V_0.pdf. Format CMD|SUB|DATA|NAME|NOTES
# Default address B6h, controller E0h. Frame FE FE <to> <from> Cn [Sc] [data] FD ; PASS(OK)=FB, FAIL(NG)=FA. Single receiver (VFO A/B): NO 29 receiver prefix, no Main/Sub, no dualwatch. Commands marked * in the manual can be set or read (read = send command without sub/data, or with channel/setting number only where needed).
# Baud rate setting only needed for the [REMOTE] jack (USB: no baud setting). Power ON (18 01) via [REMOTE] needs repeated FE before the frame: 19200:25, 9600:13, 4800:7.
# Note: when 'Cancel CI-V Remote Set Levels' = All Volume Levels, turning AF/RF/SQL knobs overrides CI-V AF/RF/SQL levels.
# FREQ = BCD 5 bytes LSB first: [10Hz 1Hz][1kHz 100Hz][100kHz 10kHz][10MHz 1MHz][1GHz 100MHz]
00||FREQ BCD 5 bytes (see p.16)|Set and output the current operating frequency (transceive)|
01||MODE bytes mode[,filter] (see p.16)|Set and output the current operating mode (transceive)|mode 00 LSB,01 USB,02 AM,03 CW,04 RTTY,05 FM,07 CW-R,08 RTTY-R; filter 01 FIL1,02 FIL2,03 FIL3; filter may be skipped (FIL1 with cmd 01)
02||BAND EDGE (see p.16): lower 5B + 2D + upper 5B|Read the current upper and lower edge frequencies|
03||FREQ BCD 5 bytes|Read the current operating frequency|
04||MODE 2 bytes mode,filter|Read the current operating mode|
05||FREQ BCD 5 bytes|Set the current operating frequency|
06||MODE bytes mode[,filter]|Set the operating mode|filter skipped: default filter of the mode
07||(none)|Switch to the VFO mode|
07|00||Switch to the VFO mode and select VFO A|
07|01||Switch to the VFO mode and select VFO B|
07|A0||Equalize VFO A and VFO B|
07|B0||Exchange VFO A with VFO B|
08||(none)|Switch to the Memory mode|
08||BCD 2 bytes 00 01 ~ 00 99|Select the Memory channel|00 01=M-CH01, 00 99=M-CH99
08||BCD 2 bytes 01 00|Select the Programmed Scan Edge channel P1|
08||BCD 2 bytes 01 01|Select the Programmed Scan Edge channel P2|
09||(none)|Store displayed contents into the selected Memory channel|
0A||(none)|Copy the selected Memory channel contents to the VFO|
0B||(none)|Clear the selected Memory channel (blank)|P1 and P2 cannot be cleared
0E|00||Stop the current scan|
0E|01||Start a Programmed or Memory scan|VFO mode: programmed scan; Memory mode: memory scan
0E|02||Start a Programmed scan|
0E|03||Start a F scan|
0E|12||Start a Fine Programmed scan|
0E|13||Start a Fine F scan|
0E|22||Start a Memory scan|
0E|23||Start a Select Memory scan|
0E|A1~A7|see p.16|Set the frequency span for F scan|A1 +-5 kHz,A2 +-10 kHz,A3 +-20 kHz,A4 +-50 kHz,A5 +-100 kHz,A6 +-500 kHz,A7 +-1 MHz
0E|B0||Release the Select Memory channel|
0E|B1||Set the channel as a Select Memory channel|
0E|B1|01 ~ 03|Set the channel as a specific Select Memory channel|01=SEL1 02=SEL2 03=SEL3
0E|B2|00 ~ 03|Set whether all or one Select Memory channel is scanned|00=ALL 01=SEL1 02=SEL2 03=SEL3
0E|D0||Turn Scan Resume OFF|
0E|D3||Turn Scan Resume (Close&Delay) ON|
0F||(none) request / reply 00/01|Read the ON/OFF status of the Split function|00=OFF 01=ON
0F|00||Turn the Split function OFF|
0F|01||Turn the Split function ON|
10||00 ~ 08|Set or read the tuning step|send/read (*); 00=OFF (10 Hz or 1 Hz),01=0.1 kHz,02=1 kHz,03=5 kHz,04=9 kHz,05=10 kHz,06=12.5 kHz,07=20 kHz,08=25 kHz; automatically 1 Hz for Fine Tuning
11||00/20|Set or read the 20 dB attenuator|send/read (*); 00=OFF 20=ON (BCD)
12|00|00/01|Set or read the receiving antenna (RX ANT) ON/OFF|send/read (*); 00=OFF 01=ON
13|00||Announce S-meter level, operating frequency and mode|S-meter not announced when S-Level SPEECH OFF (1A 05 00 44 00)
13|01||Announce S-meter level and operating frequency|
13|02||Announce the current operating mode|announced after the frequency announcement
14|01|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the AF gain|send/read (*); 00 00=min 02 55=max
14|02|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the RF gain|00 00=min 02 55=max
14|03|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the squelch level|00 00=min 02 55=max
14|05|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the peak frequency of the Audio Peak Filter|10 Hz steps; 00 00=Pitch-550 Hz 01 28=Pitch 02 55=Pitch+550 Hz
14|06|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the Noise Reduction level|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|07|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read Digital Twin PBT shift (inner: PBT1)|00 00=narrows upper freq, 01 28=center, 02 55=narrows lower freq
14|08|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read Digital Twin PBT shift (outer: PBT2)|00 00=narrows upper freq, 01 28=center, 02 55=narrows lower freq
14|09|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the CW pitch frequency|5 Hz steps; 00 00=300 Hz 01 28=600 Hz 02 55=900 Hz
14|0A|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the RF power|00 00=min 02 55=max
14|0B|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the microphone gain|00 00=min 02 55=max
14|0C|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the keying speed|00 00=6 WPM 02 55=48 WPM
14|0D|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the Notch filter setting|00 00=higher freq, 01 28=middle, 02 55=lower freq
14|0E|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the Speech Compressor level|00 00=0 02 55=10
14|0F|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the Break-in delay|00 00=2.0d 02 55=13.0d
14|12|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the Noise Blanker level|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|15|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the gain of the monitored audio (Monitor level)|00 00=0% 02 55=100%; NOTE this model has no 14 14 DRIVE and no 14 13 DIGI-SEL in the table
14|16|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the VOX sensitivity (VOX gain)|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
14|17|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the ANTI VOX sensitivity|00 00=0% 02 55=100%; higher = VOX less sensitive
14|19|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Set or read the LCD backlight brightness|00 00=0% 02 55=100%
15|01|00/01|Read Open/Closed status of Noise or S-meter squelch|00=Closed 01=Open
15|02|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read the S-meter level|00 00=S0 01 20=S9 02 41=S9+60 dB
15|05|00/01|Read Open/Closed status of the squelch (various squelch functions)|00=Closed 01=Open
15|07|00/01|Read the status of the OVF indicator|00=Not displayed 01=Displayed
15|11|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read the Po meter level|00 00=0% 01 43=50% 02 13=100%; 00 00 returned while receiving
15|12|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read the SWR meter level|00 00=SWR1.0 00 48=1.5 00 80=2.0 01 20=3.0; 00 00 while receiving
15|13|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read the ALC meter level|00 00=min 01 20=max; 00 00 while receiving
15|14|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read the COMP meter level|00 00=0 dB 01 30=15 dB 02 10=30 dB; 00 00 while receiving
15|15|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read the Vd meter level|00 00=0 V 00 13=10 V 02 41=16 V (as printed; 00 13 for 10 V looks like a manual typo, UNSURE)
15|16|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|Read the Id meter level|00 00=0 00 97=10 01 46=15 02 41=25
16|02|00 ~ 02|Set or read the preamp|send/read (*); 00=OFF 01=P.AMP1 ON 02=P.AMP2 ON
16|12|01 ~ 03|Set or read the AGC time constant|01=FAST 02=MID 03=SLOW
16|22|00/01|Set or read the Noise Blanker ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|32|00,01,02,03|Audio peak filter (APF)|00=OFF 01=WIDE ON (320 Hz if APF type SHARP) 02=MID (160 Hz) 03=NAR (80 Hz)
16|40|00/01|Set or read the Noise Reduction ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|41|00/01|Set or read the Auto Notch ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|42|00/01|Set or read the Repeater tone ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|43|00/01|Set or read the Tone squelch ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|44|00/01|Set or read the Speech Compressor ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|45|00/01|Set or read the Monitor ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|46|00/01|Set or read the VOX function ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|47|00 ~ 02|Set or read the Break-in function in CW mode|00=OFF 01=Semi 02=Full
16|48|00/01|Set or read the Manual Notch ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
16|4F|00/01|Set or read the Twin Peak Filter ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON; ON only when Mark=2125 Hz and Shift=170 Hz
16|50|00/01|Set or read the Lock function ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON; MAIN DIAL or panel locked depending on 1A 05 00 48
16|56|00/01|Set or read the IF filter shape|00=SHARP 01=SOFT
16|57|00 ~ 02|Set or read the filter width of the Manual Notch|00=WIDE 01=MID 02=NAR
16|58|00 ~ 02|Set or read the SSB transmit filter bandwidth|00=WIDE 01=MID 02=NAR; applied TBW depends on speech compressor ON/OFF (16 44): WIDE=1A 05 00 14, MID=1A 05 00 15, NAR=1A 05 00 16
16|65|00/01|Set or read the IP Plus function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|66|00/01|Set or read the TX Inhibit function|00=OFF 01=ON
17||ASCII text up to 30 chars (see p.16)|Send CW messages|sent as CW when transmitting or break-in ON in CW mode; FF stops; ^ = no inter-character space
18|00||Turn the transceiver OFF|
18|01||Turn the transceiver ON|see p.16 (FE preamble needed via REMOTE jack)
19|00||Read the transceiver ID|
1A|00|see p.17|Set or read a specific Memory channel content|send/read (*)
1A|01|see p.19|Set or read a specific band stacking register content|
1A|02|see p.19|Set or read a specific Keyer Memory content|several contest numbers allowed
1A|03|see p.19|Set or read the IF filter width|
1A|04|see p.20|Set or read the AGC time constant|
1A|05 00 01|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX / SSB] Sets or reads the RX HPF/LPF settings.|
1A|05 00 02|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX] Sets or reads the RX Tone (Bass) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 03|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX] Sets or reads the RX Tone (Treble) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 04|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX / AM] Sets or reads the RX HPF/LPF settings.|
1A|05 00 05|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX] Sets or reads the RX Tone (Bass) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 06|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX] Sets or reads the RX Tone (Treble) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 07|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX / FM] Sets or reads the RX HPF/LPF settings.|
1A|05 00 08|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX] Sets or reads the RX Tone (Bass) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 09|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX] Sets or reads the RX Tone (Treble) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 10|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX / CW] Sets or reads the RX HPF/LPF settings.|
1A|05 00 11|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > RX / RTTY] Sets or reads the RX HPF/LPF settings.|
1A|05 00 12|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX / SSB] Sets or reads the TX Tone (Bass) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 13|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX] Sets or reads the TX Tone (Treble) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 14|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX] Sets or reads the TBW (WIDE) setting.|
1A|05 00 15|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX] Sets or reads the TBW (MID) setting.|
1A|05 00 16|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX] Sets or reads the TBW (NAR) setting.|
1A|05 00 17|See p. 20.|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX / SSB-D] Sets or reads the TBW setting.|
1A|05 00 18|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX / AM] Sets or reads the TX Tone (Bass) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 19|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX] Sets or reads the TX Tone (Treble) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 20|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX / FM] Sets or reads the TX Tone (Bass) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5)
1A|05 00 21|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|[SET > Tone Control/TBW > TX] Sets or reads the TX Tone (Treble) level.|(00=-5 ~ 10=+5) 8
1A|05 00 22|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Beep Level.|(00 00=Minimum ~ 02 55=Maximum)
1A|05 00 23|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Beep Level Limit setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 24|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Beep|(Confirmation) setting. (00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 25|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 03|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Band Edge Beep setting.|(00=OFF 01=ON (Default) 02=ON (User) 03=ON (User) & TX Limit)
1A|05 00 26|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the RF/SQL Control setting.|(00=Auto, 01=SQL, 02=RF+SQL)
1A|05 00 27|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Cancel CI-V Remote Set Levels setting.|( 00=All Volume Levels, 01=Operated Volume Level)
1A|05 00 28|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the MF Band ATT setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 29|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|[SET > Function > TX Delay / HF] Sets or reads the TX Delay setting.|( 00=OFF, 01=10 ms, 02=15 ms, 03=20 ms, 04=25 ms, 05=30 ms)
1A|05 00 30|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|[SET > Function > TX Delay / 50M] Sets or reads the TX Delay setting.|( 00=OFF, 01=10 ms, 02=15 ms, 03=20 ms, 04=25 ms, 05=30 ms)
1A|05 00 31|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|[SET > Function > TX Delay / 70M] Sets or reads the TX Delay setting.|(00=OFF, 01=10 ms, 02=15 ms, 03=20 ms, 04=25 ms, 05=30 ms)
1A|05 00 32|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Time-Out Timer|(CI-V) setting. ( 00=OFF, 01=3 min, 02=5 min, 03=10 min, 04=20 min, 05=30 min) L Valid only for transmission initiated by a CI-V command or by pushing TRANSMIT on the transceiver.
1A|05 00 33|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function > SPLIT] Sets or reads the Quick SPLIT setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 34|See p. 20.|[SET > Function > SPLIT] Sets or reads the FM SPLIT Offset|(HF) setting.
1A|05 00 35|See p. 20.|[SET > Function > SPLIT] Sets or reads the FM SPLIT Offset|(50M) setting.
1A|05 00 36|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function > SPLIT] Sets or reads the SPLIT LOCK setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 37|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function > Tuner] Sets or reads the [TUNER] Switch setting.|(00=Manual, 01=Auto)
1A|05 00 38|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function > Tuner] Sets or reads the PTT Start setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 39|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the RTTY Mark Frequency setting.|( 00=1275 Hz, 01=1615 Hz, 02=2125 Hz)
1A|05 00 40|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the RTTY Shift Width setting.|(00=170 Hz, 01=200 Hz, 02=425 Hz)
1A|05 00 41|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the RTTY Keying Polarity setting.|(00=Normal, 01=Reverse)
1A|05 00 42|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function > SPEECH] Sets or reads the SPEECH Language setting.|(00=English, 01=Japanese)
1A|05 00 43|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function > SPEECH] Sets or reads the SPEECH Speed setting.|(0=Slow, 01=Fast)
1A|05 00 44|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function > SPEECH] Sets or reads the S-Level SPEECH setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 45|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function > SPEECH] Sets or reads the MODE SPEECH setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 46|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Function > SPEECH] Sets or reads the SPEECH Level setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%)
1A|05 00 47|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the [SPEECH/LOCK] Switch setting.|(00=SPEECH/LOCK, 01=LOCK/SPEECH)
1A|05 00 48|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Lock Function setting.|( 00=MAIN DIAL, 01=PANEL) L When PANEL is selected, keys and dials are also locked except for AF RF/SQL , AF RF/SQL , POWER , and SPEECH .
1A|05 00 49|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Memo Pad Quantity setting.|(00=5 ch, 01=10 ch)
1A|05 00 50|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the MAIN DIAL Auto TS setting.|(00=OFF, 01=Low, 02=High)
1A|05 00 51|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the MIC Up/Down Speed setting.|(00=Slow, 01=Fast)
1A|05 00 52|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Quick RIT/TX Clear setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 53|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the [NOTCH] Switch|(SSB) setting. ( 00=Auto, 01=Manual, 02=Auto/Manual)
1A|05 00 54|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the [NOTCH] Switch|(AM) setting. ( 00=Auto, 01=Manual, 02=Auto/Manual)
1A|05 00 55|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the SSB/CW Synchronous Tuning setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 56|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the CW Normal Side setting.|(00=LSB, 01=USB)
1A|05 00 57|See p. 21.|[SET > Function > Front Key Customize] Sets or reads the [VOX/BK-IN] setting.|
1A|05 00 58|See p. 23.|[SET > Function > Front Key Customize] Sets or reads the [AUTOTUNE] setting.|
1A|05 00 59|See p. 21.|[SET > Function > Front Key Customize] Sets or reads the [] setting.|
1A|05 00 60|See p. 21.|[SET > Function > Front Key Customize] Sets or reads the [] setting.|
1A|05 00 61|See p. 21.|[SET > Function > MIC Key Customize] Sets or reads the [UP] setting.|
1A|05 00 62|See p. 21.|[SET > Function > MIC Key Customize] Sets or reads the [DN] setting.|
1A|05 00 63|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Screen Capture [POWER] SW setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 64|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Screen Capture File Type setting.|(00=PNG, 01=BMP)
1A|05 00 65|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Keyboard Type setting.|(00=Ten-key, 01=Full Keyboard)
1A|05 00 66|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Full Keyboard Layout setting.|(00=English, 01=German, 02=French)
1A|05 00 67|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the Calibration Marker setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 68|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Function] Sets or reads the REF Adjust setting.|(00 00=0%, 02 55=100%)
1A|05 00 69|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > USB AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the Output Select setting.|(00=AF, 01=IF)
1A|05 00 70|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Connectors > USB AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the AF Output Level setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%)
1A|05 00 71|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > USB AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the AF SQL setting.|(00=OFF (Open), 01=ON)
1A|05 00 72|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > USB AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the AF Beep/Speech... Output setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 73|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Connectors > USB AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the IF Output Level setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%) 9
1A|05 00 74|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the Output Select setting.|(00=AF, 01=IF)
1A|05 00 75|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the AF Output Level setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%)
1A|05 00 76|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the AF SQL setting.|(00=OFF (Open), 01=ON)
1A|05 00 77|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the AF Beep/Speech... Output setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 78|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the IF Output Level setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%)
1A|05 00 79|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > LAN AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the Output Select setting.|(00=AF, 01=IF)
1A|05 00 80|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > LAN AF/IF Output] Sets or reads the AF SQL setting.|(00=OFF (Open), 01=ON)
1A|05 00 81|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Connectors > MOD Input] Sets or reads the USB MOD Level setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%)
1A|05 00 82|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Connectors > MOD Input] Sets or reads the ACC MOD Level setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%)
1A|05 00 83|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 55|[SET > Connectors > MOD Input] Sets or reads the LAN MOD Level setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%)
1A|05 00 84|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|[SET > Connectors > MOD Input] Sets or reads the DATA OFF MOD setting.|( 00=MIC, 01=USB, 02=ACC, 03=MIC, USB, 04=MIC, ACC 05=LAN)
1A|05 00 85|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|[SET > Connectors > MOD Input] Sets or reads the DATA MOD setting.|( 00=MIC, 01=USB, 02=ACC, 03=MIC, USB, 04=MIC, ACC 05=LAN)
1A|05 00 86|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > External Keypad] Sets or reads the VOICE setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 87|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > External Keypad] Sets or reads the KEYER setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 88|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > External Keypad] Sets or reads the RTTY setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 89|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > CI-V] Sets or reads the CI-V Transceive setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 90|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 23|[SET > Connectors > CI-V] Sets or reads the USB/LANREMOTE Transceive Address setting.|(00 00=00h ~ 02 23=DFh)
1A|05 00 91|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > CI-V] Sets or reads the CI-V Output (for ANT) setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 92|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > CI-V] Sets or reads the CI-V USB (A) Echo Back setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 93|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors > CI-V] Sets or reads the CI-V USB (B) Echo Back setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 94|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors] Sets or reads the USB (B) Function setting.|(00=RTTY Decode, 01=CI-V)
1A|05 00 95|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SET > Connectors] Sets or reads the SEND Relay Output setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 96|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 04|[SET > Connectors > USB SEND/Keying] Sets or reads the the USB SEND setting.|(00=OFF, 01=USB (A) DTR, 02=USB (A) RTS, 03=USB (B) DTR 04=USB (B) RTS) L USB (A) and USB (B) are the 2 virtual COM ports on the [USB] port on the rear panel. L You cannot select the same terminal used for USB Keying (CW) or USB Keying (RTTY) setting.
