1A|05 02 37|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > TX MEM > EDIT/SET > 001 SET] Sets or reads the Count Up Trigger|(RT3) setting. (00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 38|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > TX MEM > EDIT/SET > 001 SET] Sets or reads the Count Up Trigger|(RT4) setting. (00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 39|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > TX MEM > EDIT/SET > 001 SET] Sets or reads the Count Up Trigger|(RT5) setting. (00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 40|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > TX MEM > EDIT/SET > 001 SET] Sets or reads the Count Up Trigger|(RT6) setting. (00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 41|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > TX MEM > EDIT/SET > 001 SET] Sets or reads the Count Up Trigger|(RT7) setting. (00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 42|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > TX MEM > EDIT/SET > 001 SET] Sets or reads the Count Up Trigger|(RT8) setting. (00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 43|BCD 2 bytes 00 01 ~ 99 99|[RTTY DECODE > TX MEM > EDIT/SET > 001 SET] Sets or reads the Present Number setting.|(00 01=1 ~ 99 99=9999)
1A|05 02 44|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > < 1 > > LOG] Sets or reads the Decode Log setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 45|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > < 1 > > LOG > Log Set] Sets or reads the File Type setting.|(00=Text, 01=HTML)
1A|05 02 46|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > < 1 > > LOG > Log Set] Sets or reads the Time Stamp setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 47|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > < 1 > > LOG > Log Set] Sets or reads the Time Stamp (Time) setting.|(00=Local, 01=UTC)
1A|05 02 48|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RTTY DECODE > < 1 > > LOG > Log Set] Sets or reads the Time Stamp|(Frequency) setting. (00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 49|See p. 22.|[CW DECODE SET:  KEYER/DECODE > CW DECODE > SET] Sets or reads the FFT Scope Waveform Color setting.|
1A|05 02 50|See p. 22.|[CW DECODE SET:  KEYER/DECODE > CW DECODE > SET] Sets or reads the Signal Level Waveform Color setting.|
1A|05 02 51|See p. 22.|[CW DECODE SET:  KEYER/DECODE > CW DECODE > SET] Sets or reads the Font Color|(Receive) setting.
1A|05 02 52|See p. 22.|[CW DECODE SET:  KEYER/DECODE > CW DECODE > SET] Sets or reads the Font Color|(Transmit) setting.
1A|05 02 53|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SCAN SET: SCAN > SET] Sets or read the SCAN Speed setting.|(00=Slow, 01=Fast)
1A|05 02 54|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[SCAN SET: SCAN > SET] Sets or reads the SCAN Resume setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON) 14
1A|05 02 55|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 25|[VOICE TX: VOICE > TX LEVEL] Sets or reads the TX LEVEL setting.|(00 00=0% ~ 02 55=100%)
1A|05 02 56|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[VOICE TX SET: VOICE > REC/SET > SET] Sets or reads the Auto Monitor setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 57|BCD 1 byte 01 ~ 15|[VOICE TX SET: VOICE > REC/SET > SET] Sets or reads the Repeat Time setting.|(01=1 sec. ~ 15=15 sec.)
1A|05 02 58|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RECORD > Recorder Set] Sets or reads the TX REC Audio setting.|(00=Direct, 01=Monitor)
1A|05 02 59|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RECORD > Recorder Set] Sets or reads the RX REC Condition setting.|(00=Always, 01=Squelch Auto)
1A|05 02 60|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RECORD > Recorder Set] Sets or reads the File Split setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 61|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[RECORD > Recorder Set] Sets or reads the PTT Auto REC setting.|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 02 62|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 03|[RECORD > Recorder Set] Sets or reads the PRE-REC for PTT Auto REC setting.|( 00=OFF, 01=5 sec, 02=10 sec, 03=15 sec)
1A|05 02 63|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 03|[RECORD > Player Set] Sets or reads the Skip Time setting.|( 00=3 sec, 01=5 sec, 02=10 sec, 03=30 sec)
1A|05 02 64|See p. 22.|[MENU SET:] Sets or reads the CW [KEYER/DECODE] Key setting.|(00=Select screen, 01=KEYER (Hold down: Select screen), 02=DECODE (Hold down: Select screen))
1A|05 02 65|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 09|[NB: FUNCTION > NB (Touch for 1 second)] Sets or reads the DEPTH setting.|(00=1 ~ 09=10)
1A|05 02 66|BCD 2 bytes 00 00 ~ 02 25|[NB: FUNCTION > NB (Touch for 1 second)] Sets or reads the WIDTH setting.|(00 00=1 ~ 02 55=100)
1A|05 02 67|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 20|[VOX: FUNCTION > VOX (Touch for 1 second)] Sets or reads the Delay setting.|( 00=0.0 sec. ~ 20=2.0 sec. in 0.1 sec. steps)
1A|05 02 68|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 03|[VOX: FUNCTION > VOX (Touch for 1 second)] Sets or reads the Voice delay setting.|( 00=OFF, 01=Short, 02=Mid, 03=Long)
1A|05 02 69|BCD 1 byte 00/01|[APF: FUNCTION > 2 > APF (Touch for 1 second)] Sets or reads the TYPE setting.|(00=SHARP, 01=SOFT)
1A|05 02 70|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 06|[APF: FUNCTION > 2 > APF (Touch for 1 second)] Sets or reads the AF LEVEL setting.|(00=0 dB ~ 06=6 dB)
1A|06|see p.22|Set or read the DATA mode and filter width settings|
1A|07|00/01|Set or read the NTP server access|00=Terminate 01=Initiate
1A|08|00 ~ 02|Read the NTP server access result|00=Accessing/not accessed since power ON 01=Successful 02=Failed (also when synchronisation stopped by 1A 07 00); 00 returned just after power ON
1B|00|see p.23|Set or read the Repeater tone frequency|
1B|01|see p.23|Set or read the TSQL tone frequency|
1C|00|00/01|Set or read the RX/TX status of the transceiver (PTT)|00=RX 01=TX; auto output on change when CI-V Output (for ANT) ON (1C 04 01)
1C|01|00 ~ 02|Set or read the internal antenna tuner status|00=OFF 01=ON 02=Tune
1C|02|00/01|Set or read XFC (transmit frequency monitor)|00=OFF 01=ON
1C|03|see p.16|Read the transmit frequency|auto output on change if 1C 04 01; cannot be set
1C|04|00/01|Set or read the CI-V Output (for ANT)|00=OFF 01=ON
1E|00||Read the number of available TX frequency bands|
1E|01|see p.16|Read upper and lower edge frequencies of a TX frequency band|
1E|02||Read the maximum number of User Band Edges|returns 30
1E|03|see p.16|Set or read upper and lower edge frequencies of a User Band Edge|send/read (*)
21|00|see p.23|Set or read the RIT frequency|1Hz/10Hz/100Hz/1kHz digits + sign 00=+ 01=-
21|01|00/01|Set or read the RIT function ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
21|02|00/01|Set or read the TX (delta TX) function ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
25||see p.23: byte 00=Selected VFO 01=Unselected VFO + FREQ 5 bytes|Set or read the operating frequency of the Selected or Unselected VFO|send/read (*)
26||see p.24: byte 00/01 + mode + data mode 00=OFF 01=ON + filter 01-03|Set or read operating mode, data mode and IF filter width of the Selected or Unselected VFO|send/read (*); data/filter can be skipped
27|00|see p.24|Output the scope waveform data to the controller|only if 27 10 and 27 11 ON
27|10|00/01|Set or read the spectrum scope ON/OFF|00=OFF 01=ON
27|11|00/01|Set or read scope waveform data output to PC|00=OFF 01=ON; only via USB or LAN
27|12|00 (Main only)|Set or read the Main or Sub scope|
27|13|00 (Single only)|Set or read Single or Dual scope|
27|14|see p.25|Set or read scope mode|00=Center 01=Fixed 02=SCROLL-C 03=SCROLL-F
27|15|see p.25|Set or read Span (Center/SCROLL-C)|
27|16|see p.25|Set or read Scope Edge Number (Fixed/SCROLL-F)|
27|17|see p.25|Set or read Scope Hold ON/OFF|
27|19|see p.25|Set or read Scope Reference level|
27|1A|see p.25|Set or read Scope Sweep speed|
27|1B|00/01|Set or read Scope during Tx (CENTER TYPE)|00=OFF 01=ON
27|1C|00 ~ 02|Set or read CENTER Type Display|00=Filter Center 01=Carrier Point Center 02=Carrier Point Center (Abs. Freq.)
27|1D|see p.25|Set or read Scope VBW|
27|1E|see p.26|Set or read Scope Fixed Edge frequencies|
27|20|00/01|Set or read Marker Position (FIX Type/SCROLL Type)|00=Filter Center 01=Carrier Point
28|00|00|Stop the Voice TX memory transmission|
28|00|01 ~ 08|Start a Voice TX memory transmission|01=T1 ~ 08=T8
